 ],
 "literal": "Ayirai fish spread beautiful cool agricultural field's / eminent beauty blossoming hollow-stemmed round-stalked / water lilies pluckers, desiring water, like that, she / between breasts lying, shivering you became / worshipping-and-seeing crescent moon like appearing, we to you / difficult-to-attain became time / greatly you appeared; I grieve indeed!",
 "translation": "In the beautiful, cool fields where ayirai fish spread, those who pluck the water lilies with eminent beauty, hollow stems, and round stalks, thirst for water even while standing in it. In the same way, though you lay between her breasts, you never stopped shivering with desire. But in those days when we were as rare to you as the crescent moon that people worship upon seeing, you appeared before us constantly. Now, I can only grieve!",
 "modern": "அயிரை மீன்கள் பரவியுள்ள அழகிய குளிர்ந்த வயல்களில், உயர்ந்த அழகுடன், துளையுள்ள தடித்த தண்டுகளைக் கொண்ட ஆம்பல் மலர்களைப் பறிப்பவர்கள், நீரினுள்ளே நின்றுகொண்டே நீருக்காக ஏங்குவது போல, இவளுடைய மார்புகளுக்கு இடையே கிடந்தும் நீங்கள் தணியாத ஆசையால் நடுங்கினீர்கள். மக்கள் தொழுது பார்க்கும் பிறை நிலவைப் போல நாங்கள் உங்களுக்குக் காண்பதற்கு அரியவர்களாக இருந்த காலத்தில், நீங்கள் அடிக்கடி எங்கள் முன்னால் வந்து தோன்றினீர்கள். இப்போது இவள் உங்களோடு இருக்கும்போது நீங்கள் விலகிச் செல்வதை எண்ணி நான் வருந்துகிறேன்.",
 "explanation": "The confidante (தோழி) is speaking to the hero (தலைவன்) who has returned from his tryst or is neglecting the heroine after marriage. She contrasts his past behavior with his present indifference. In the past, when the heroine was hard to reach (like the rare crescent moon), he was always present, seeking her. Now, even when he is with her, he seems unsatisfied or distant, like people standing in water plucking lilies but still thirsting for water. The image of the water-lily pluckers standing in the cool water of the agricultural field (Marutam landscape) but still thirsting for water represents the hero's insatiable desire or his strange dissatisfaction even when he has the heroine close to him. The comparison of the heroine to the crescent moon highlights how precious and rare she once was to him.",
